                                    <h1>HRMS Development for India &amp; Global Companies 2026</h1>
                                    <p>HRMS is where growing companies feel operational pain earliest — leaves in Excel, payroll in outdated software, no performance data, poor exit workflows. India-headquartered companies with UAE / USA / UK / AU teams have an extra challenge: local compliance in every country. Here is what a modern HRMS should do and how <a href='https://www.itdgrowthlabs.com/index.php'>ITD GrowthLabs</a> builds or configures them.</p>
                                    <h2>HRMS Coverage: The 10 Modules</h2>
                                    <ol><li>Employee master + org structure</li><li>Leave + attendance</li><li>Payroll (region-specific)</li><li>Performance management (PMS)</li><li>Recruitment / ATS</li><li>Onboarding + offboarding</li><li>Learning management (LMS)</li><li>Expense management</li><li>Compliance filings (region-specific)</li><li>Analytics + reporting</li></ol>
                                    <h2>India Payroll Compliance: What Actually Matters</h2>
                                    <p>India payroll is complex: TDS (Section 192), PF (12% employer + 12% employee subject to limits), ESIC (for salaries ≤ ₹21,000), Professional Tax (state-specific), Gratuity (after 5 years), Bonus Act, Labour Welfare Fund. New: Code on Wages 2019 (partially implemented). Any HRMS you use — off-shelf or custom — must handle all of this correctly. Missing PF filings alone can create ₹lakhs in penalties.</p>
                                    <h2>Multi-Country Payroll: The Real Options</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Option A: Local payroll provider per country</strong> — Zoho / RazorpayX / Keka for India; Bayzat / Paylocity for UAE; ADP for USA; Sage for UK. Integrate each into HRMS via API. Best control, most integration work.</p><p><strong>Option B: Global provider</strong> — Deel, Remote, Papaya Global handle 100+ countries. Higher cost, less control, less local nuance.</p><p><strong>Option C: Off-shelf HRMS with multi-country payroll built in</strong> — Workday (enterprise), Darwinbox (India-first with strong UAE / SEA), BambooHR + integrations. Balance of control and simplicity.</p>
                                    <h2>Cost Bands</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Off-shelf SMB HRMS:</strong> ₹100-400/employee/month (India), $8-25/employee/month (international).</p><p><strong>Off-shelf enterprise HRMS:</strong> Workday, SAP SuccessFactors, Oracle HCM — ₹800-3,500/employee/month.</p><p><strong>Custom HRMS:</strong> ₹35 lakh - 1.8 Cr / $42K-215K build cost, 16-36 weeks, then hosting + maintenance.</p>
                                    <h2>When Custom HRMS Makes Sense</h2>
                                    <p>Rarely, but sometimes. Good fits: (1) staffing / consulting firms with unique bill-rate + timesheet logic, (2) large field-force organizations with heavy shift / attendance complexity, (3) manufacturing with complex incentive / piece-rate payroll, (4) companies with 5,000+ employees who want deep customization at lower per-user cost than Workday.</p>
                                    <h2>What to Ship in Year One</h2>
                                    <p>Employee master, leaves, payroll (region-specific), performance basics (KRA / OKR), and a solid mobile app for employees. Ship the remaining 5 modules over year 2. Trying to do all 10 in year 1 is how HRMS projects fail.</p>

